<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "A registered nickname is a name and a password, and nothing else is required. Adding an address is optional, and what it buys is one thing: a way back in if the password is gone. Without it, a forgotten password means losing the nickname until it is released for disuse."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lock}>{dgettext("help_games", "Who can see it")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "Nobody. It is not shown in your profile, not in WHOIS, not to channel operators and not to the person you are talking to. It is used to send you a link and for nothing else — no digest, no announcements, no “we miss you”."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_shield}>{dgettext("help_games", "Adding and confirming one")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "Open the Account window from the Start menu and type it in. A link arrives; following it confirms the address. Until you follow that link the address counts for nothing — in particular, no password reset will be sent to it. That is what stops somebody typing an address they do not own."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_question}>{dgettext("help_games", "Forgetting your password")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "On the Connect screen, after typing your nickname, press “I forgot my password”. The answer is the same whatever you type — a nickname with an address, one without, one that does not exist — because any other answer would let somebody read the register one guess at a time. If there was an address to send to, a link arrives and is good for a day."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_clock}>{dgettext("help_games", "Before a nickname is released")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "Nicknames left unused are released so somebody else can take them. If you confirmed an address, you are told about two weeks beforehand, and signing in once is all it takes to keep it."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_reject}>{dgettext("help_games", "Removing it")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "The same Account window removes it, and removing it also cancels any link already sent. A server whose operator never configured outgoing mail does not offer any of this: there is no address field and no recovery link, because there would be nowhere to send."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_games", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="feature-sessions">
    {dgettext("help_games", "Signing In On Several Screens")}
  </.help_link>
  | <.help_link topic="cmd-ns">{dgettext("help_games", "NickServ")}</.help_link>
</p>
